- **Copy detection:** the figures use `-w -M -C`. The tool printed no copy-detection note.
- **Bus factor:** it is 1 on this file. Troy alone holds 67.3% of the lines. It takes 3 authors to reach 80%.
  - Bus factor here means the fewest authors whose surviving lines reach 50%.
  - Without the reformat correction, it is still 1, with Troy at 57.5%.
- **Whole repository:** across all 18 files, Troy Goode (both addresses) holds 649 lines (39.0%) and Douglas Christopher Wilson holds 551 (33.2%). The repository bus factor is 2, with 4 authors needed to reach 80%. So `lib/index.js` is more concentrated in Troy than the rest of the repository.

Line counts show whose code survives. They don't show review work, design discussion, or code that was deleted on purpose.

